    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0124" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/775a Suppl.: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Representatives
                        in Certain American Republics </hi><anchor n="60" xml:id="d129-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-09T21:00:00-04:00">September 9,
                            1942—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s circular telegram of June 29<anchor n="61" xml:id="d129-f2"/>
                    referred to supplies being reduced to something less than 50 percent of 1941
                    consumption.</p>
                <p>You should now advise the country to which you are accredited that the present
                    basis for scheduling supplies is forty percent of 1941 consumption plus any war
                    essential requirements approved through the procedure outlined in our circular
                    telegram of July 25 and amended by Department’s circular telegram of September
                        3.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d129-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d129-f1" n="60" type="source" xml:id="d129-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to representatives in Chile, Bolivia, Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, Paraguay,
                    Uruguay, and Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d129-f2" n="61" xml:id="d129-f2-content">
                <p>See footnote 49, <ref target="#pg104">p. 104</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d129-f3" n="62" xml:id="d129-f3-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
